(Chemical Kinetics, Reaction Coordinates and Temperature Dependence) Tj T*
(Department of Physical Chemistry - Chemical Dynamics Lecture Series) Tj T*
(1. Rate Laws and Reaction Order) Tj T*
(For reaction aA + bB -> cC + dD, the experimental rate law takes the general form:) Tj T*
(Rate = k * [A]^m * [B]^n) Tj T*
(The reaction orders m and n must be determined empirically and cannot be inferred from stoichiometry.) Tj T*
(2. The Arrhenius Equation) Tj T*
(The temperature dependence of the reaction rate constant k is modeled by the Arrhenius equation:) Tj T*
(k = A * exp\(-E_a / \(R * T\)\)) Tj T*
(where A is the pre-exponential frequency factor, E_a is the activation energy in J/mol,) Tj T*
(R is the universal gas constant \(8.314 J/\(mol K\)\), and T is absolute temperature in Kelvin.) Tj T*
(Linearization of the Arrhenius relation yields the standard diagnostic plot:) Tj T*
(ln\(k\) = ln\(A\) - \(E_a / R\) * \(1 / T\)) Tj T*
(Plotting ln\(k\) vs 1/T produces a straight line whose slope is -E_a / R.) Tj T*
(Table 1: Kinetic rate constants for ester hydrolysis across temperature range.) Tj T*
(Temperature \(K\) | 1/T \(10^-3 K^-1\) | k \(M^-1 s^-1\) | ln\(k\)) Tj T*
(283.15          | 3.532            | 0.00142       | -6.557) Tj T*
(298.15          | 3.354            | 0.00512       | -5.275) Tj T*
(313.15          | 3.193            | 0.01680       | -4.086) Tj T*
(328.15          | 3.047            | 0.05040       | -2.988) Tj T*
(Figure 1 \(Page 1\): Arrhenius plot of ln\(k\) versus inverse temperature showing linear activation slope.) Tj T*
